# Code Quality Rules

1. Test Coverage:
   - Before attempting completion, always make sure that any code changes have test coverage
   - Ensure all tests pass before submitting changes

2. Lint Rules:
   - Never disable any lint rules without explicit user approval
   - If a lint rule needs to be disabled, ask the user first and explain why
   - Prefer fixing the underlying issue over disabling the lint rule
   - Document any approved lint rule disabling with a comment explaining the reason

# Adding a New Setting

To add a new setting that persists its state, follow the steps in cline_docs/settings.md

3. Code Optimization:
   - Before making any code changes, always analyze the code to understand its performance and identify areas of improvement
   - When making changes, focus on fixing bugs and optimizing performance only
   - Avoid making unnecessary code changes or adding new features without explicit user approval
   - When adding new features, ensure they are thoroughly tested and optimized for performance

4. Flutter Support:
   - In the settings, add a feature to detect if the user is developing a Flutter app/tool
   - If the user selects the Flutter option, use the Flutter SDK to create the app/tool
   - Optimize the app/tool for Flutter performance
   - Add a checkbox to the UI, next to the profile, to allow the user to select/deselect the Flutter option
